    "notes": "ScVals handed to an sdk conversion into its address type. values that are no address (void, bool, u32, a string or bytes that look like an account, a vec holding an address) must be refused, not crash; account, contract and muxed account addresses give their strkey; claimable balance and liquidity pool addresses may give their strkey or be refused. soroban-sdk 28.0.0 and 29.0.1 MuxedAddress::try_from_val panics with \"incorrect scval type\" on the first six (rs-soroban-sdk#2090, fixed on main by #2099 after 29.0.1)",
